Here are both approaches for navigating from `ProductListPage` to `ProductDetailsPage`:

## 1. Register the Route

```csharp
// AppShell.xaml.cs
public AppShell()
{
    InitializeComponent();
    Routing.RegisterRoute("productdetails", typeof(ProductDetailsPage));
}
```

## 2. Navigate from ProductListPage

**Approach A — String query parameter (product ID only):**

```csharp
// In ProductListViewModel or code-behind
async void OnProductSelected(Product product)
{
    await Shell.Current.GoToAsync($"productdetails?productId={product.Id}");
}
```

**Approach B — Full object via `ShellNavigationQueryParameters`:**

```csharp
async void OnProductSelected(Product product)
{
    var parameters = new ShellNavigationQueryParameters
    {
        { "product", product }
    };
    await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("productdetails", parameters);
}
```

## 3. Receive Data with IQueryAttributable

```csharp
public partial class ProductDetailsViewModel : ObservableObject, IQueryAttributable
{
    [ObservableProperty]
    private Product _product;

    [ObservableProperty]
    private string _productId;

    public void ApplyQueryAttributes(IDictionary<string, object> query)
    {
        // Approach B: full object passed
        if (query.TryGetValue("product", out var obj) && obj is Product p)
        {
            Product = p;
        }
        // Approach A: string ID passed — load from service
        else if (query.TryGetValue("productId", out var id))
        {
            ProductId = id.ToString();
            // Load full product asynchronously
            _ = LoadProductAsync(ProductId);
        }
    }

    private async Task LoadProductAsync(string id)
    {
        Product = await _productService.GetByIdAsync(id);
    }
}
```

## Key Points

| | Query string | ShellNavigationQueryParameters |
|---|---|---|
| **Data** | Primitive/string only | Any object |
| **Serialization** | URL-encoded | None (passed by reference) |
| **Use when** | Simple IDs, deep links | Complex objects already in memory |

Both arrive in the same `ApplyQueryAttributes` dictionary — you just check which key is present. Always `await` your `GoToAsync` calls to avoid race conditions.
